CHAPTER I 

INTRODUCTION 

 

Background Information: 

DawaiSamjho is a web-based pharmaceutical assistance system designed to make medicine-related information easily understandable and accessible to everyone. In India, many people, especially elderly individuals and rural populations, face difficulties understanding the English instructions printed on medicine strips and prescriptions.This project uses Optical Character Recognition (OCR) technology to scan medicine strips and identify medicine names. It provides simplified medicine information in Hindi and English, voice assistance, generic medicine price comparisons, drug interaction alerts, and medicine expiry tracking. The main aim is to improve medicine awareness and help users find affordable generic alternatives  

1.2 Project Objectives: 

The main objectives of the DawaiSamjho project are: 

To identify medicine names from images using OCR technology. 

To provide simplified medicine information in Hindi and English. 

To implement text-to-speech functionality for better accessibility. 

To detect duplicate active ingredients and potential drug interactions. 

To compare branded medicines with available generic alternatives. 

To help users locate nearby Jan Aushadhi stores. 

To maintain digital medicine records and track expiry dates. 

To develop a user-friendly and responsive web application using the MERN stack. 

1.3 Significance of the Project: 

The DawaiSamjho project provides several benefits to users: 

Easy Medicine Understanding: Helps users understand medicine information in simple language. 

Language Support: Provides Hindi and English information for better accessibility. 

Voice Assistance: Helps elderly and visually impaired users listen to medicine details. 

Affordable Medicines: Creates awareness about low-cost generic medicine alternatives. 

Medication Safety: Identifies duplicate salts and provides potential drug interaction alerts. 

Digital Management: Helps users maintain medicine records and monitor expiry dates. 

