CHAPTER IV 

METHODOLOGY 

4.1 Project Overview: 

4.1 Project Overview 

DawaiSamjho is a web-based pharmaceutical assistance system developed using the MERN stack. The main purpose of this project is to help users identify medicines and understand their information easily.The system uses Tesseract.js OCR technology to extract medicine names from images. After identification, it provides medicine details in Hindi and English. It also includes generic medicine price comparison, salt-based interaction checking, voice assistance, Jan Aushadhi store locator, and digital medicine management. 

The application consists of three main layers: 

Presentation Layer: React.js and Tailwind CSS are used to develop the user interface. 

Application Layer: Node.js and Express.js handle application logic and API requests. 

Data Layer: MongoDB stores medicine information, active ingredients, prices, and user records. 

4.2 Operational Feasibility 

Operational feasibility determines whether the proposed system can be easily used and operated by users. 

DawaiSamjho is designed with a simple and user-friendly interface. Users can access the application through smartphones, tablets, and computers. 

The system provides easy medicine scanning. 

Hindi and English language support improves accessibility. 

Voice assistance helps users understand medicine information. 

The digital medicine cabinet helps manage medicine records. 

Open-source technologies reduce development costs. 

Therefore, the proposed system is operationally feasible and suitable for general users. 

 

 

4.3 Research Design or Approach 

The project follows a systematic development approach to design and implement different modules. 

The major development steps are: 

