Database Integration: Connecting MongoDB for storing and retrieving medicine information. 

4.4 Data Collection Methods 

Data collection is an important part of the DawaiSamjho project because accurate medicine information is required for proper system functionality. 

The following methods are considered: 

Medicine Information: Collecting medicine names and details from reliable pharmaceutical sources. 

Active Ingredients: Gathering information about active pharmaceutical ingredients and salt compositions. 

Generic Medicine Data: Collecting branded and generic medicine names with their available prices. 

Usage Information: Collecting general medicine usage instructions and precautions from verified sources. 

Store Information: Gathering Jan Aushadhi store names, addresses, and geographical locations. 

4.5 Data Analysis Techniques 

The system uses different techniques to process and analyze medicine-related information. 

OCR Processing: Tesseract.js extracts text from medicine strip images. 

Image Preprocessing: Grayscale conversion and contrast adjustment improve image readability. 

Fuzzy Matching: Levenshtein distance helps match medicine names even when OCR produces spelling errors. 

Salt Normalization: Identifies medicines having matching active ingredients. 

Price Comparison: Compares available branded and generic medicine prices. 

Interaction Checking: Uses predefined pharmaceutical interaction rules to identify potentially unsafe combinations. 

4.6 Ethical Considerations 

The DawaiSamjho project considers user privacy, data security, and the reliability of pharmaceutical information. 

User information should be protected through secure authentication. 

Medicine information should be collected from reliable sources. 

Personal medicine records should remain confidential. 

The system should avoid providing misleading medical information. 

Drug interaction alerts should be based on verified data. 

Users should be advised to consult qualified healthcare professionals before changing their medication. 

4.7 Limitations 

Although DawaiSamjho provides several useful features, it has certain limitations: 

OCR accuracy may be affected by blurry images, poor lighting, or damaged medicine packaging. 

The system depends on the availability and accuracy of the medicine database. 

Generic medicine prices and availability may change over time. 

Initially, the application supports only Hindi and English. 

Internet connectivity is required for database access and online services. 

Drug interaction results depend on the available verified interaction database. 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

